WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.500
07:40 — Morning vault. Pharmacy keys in one hand, Ayesha opens VaultCap on her iPhone — three expiries this month, including a school passport she would have found in a drawer too late.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:17.000
12:15 — Documents find. Between customers a phone search finds the passport scan in seconds; she texts the school office without leaving the counter or digging through WhatsApp.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.500
18:30 — Family on iPad. Kitchen iPad after school runs: husband’s profile separate, kids’ docs labeled, everything still on-device — no family Dropbox argument.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:34.000
20:10 — Banks glance. Laptop for a calm look at sample bank accounts before Ramadan planning; numbers illustrative, tone quiet, no tipping or advice.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.500
21:00 — Zakat summary. Same laptop shows a Zakat summary from holdings so she can email the accountant without photographing paper ledgers.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:51.000
21:40 — Reminders set. Phone locks with renewal reminders confirmed. Drawers stay drawers. The vault stays the vault.

